			ROX-Filer
			A RISC OS-like filer for X
			by Thomas Leonard

ROX-Filer is a simple and easy to use graphical file manager for X11, the
windowing system used on Unix and Unix-like operating systems. It is also
the core component of the ROX Desktop:

	http://rox.sourceforge.net

To compile:
	$ ROX-Filer/AppRun --compile

To install:
	$ ./install.sh

To run the installed file manager:
	$ ROX-Filer

To start the new native desktop mode directly from the binary:
	$ ROX-Filer --desktop

ROX Desktop manages the wallpaper, the real XDG Desktop directory and
detected drives. Right-click an empty area of the desktop to change the
wallpaper, open the Desktop folder or refresh the desktop.

The classic pinboard and panel command-line options remain available only for
legacy compatibility while the new desktop mode is completed.


